//RS /// Validate every `--flag` in argv against the registry. The first unknown flag
//RS /// teaches E2102 (with a suggestion) and exits usage.
//RS ///
//RS /// `subcmd` is the subcommand being run (e.g. `"run"`, `"test"`). When the
//RS /// subcommand can forward args to a program, the Fix line also teaches the `--`
//RS /// separator form (D-CLI1=A).
